UPDATE lessons SET title='Year 4, Week 30, Lesson 1: Performing our compositions', data=json_patch(data,'{"child_mission":"Performing compositions needs a setlist order, instrument/tech check and a simple stage plot showing who stands where and which device is used. Do a soundcheck at performance volume. Have a backup unplugged version if tech fails.","coming_soon":null,"duration_minutes":55,"evidence_instructions":"Save the independent response, specific revisions and both short-answer explanations; record oral evidence for speaking tasks.","explicit_teaching":null,"extension":"Apply the same arts idea to a new artwork or performance, then compare two choices for clarity of effect.","follow_up_challenges":null,"guided_practice":"PRACTISE BEFORE READING THE FEEDBACK\nWrite a two-item setlist with one tech-check item and one backup plan.\n\nFEEDBACK\nStrong answer: Ordered pieces, ''test speaker'', ''sing unaccompanied if app fails.''\n\nWATCH FOR\nFirst hearing the mix onstage with an audience waiting. Soundcheck earlier.","hoard_words":null,"independent_task":"INDEPENDENT EVIDENCE\nPerform your composition with setlist and tech check complete. Note what the backup plan was even if unused.\n\nWrite a short reflection naming one artistic choice you changed and why. Movement or instrument work is optional, adult-supervised and can be described instead.","interactive_activities":null,"learning_area":"Creative Arts","learning_intention":"Performing compositions needs a setlist order, instrument/tech check and a simple stage plot showing who stands where and which device is used. Do a soundcheck at performance volume. Have a backup unplugged version if tech fails.","lesson_number":1,"lesson_role":"Explore and learn","materials":["Paper or typed answer space","Pencil","Optional: scrap paper, crayons, safe classroom instruments or clear movement space with an adult nearby"],"offline_alternative":"Use paper and pencil to complete the original task, then retain a photograph or short parent observation as evidence.","outcome_codes":["CA2-MUS-01"],"parent_notes":"Parent: Marking guidance for the independent task: Perform your composition with setlist and tech check complete. Note what the backup plan was even if unused. Accept equivalent original responses that show the same skill.\n\nParent: Written model 1: Original response on new material: Strong answer: Ordered pieces, ''test speaker'', ''sing unaccompanied if app fails.'' Reasoning: I used compose performance by attending to setlist rather than copying the worked model.\n\nParent: Written model 2: Common error: First hearing the mix onstage with an audience waiting. Soundcheck earlier. Correction: Strong answer: Ordered pieces, ''test speaker'', ''sing unaccompanied if app fails.'' Why: the correction restores accurate use of compose performance.\n\nParent: Likely misconception: First hearing the mix onstage with an audience waiting. Soundcheck earlier. Keep sample answers out of the child role.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 1: Produce a fresh example demonstrating compose performance on new material (not the worked model). Explain the particular words, sources or choices that make it work.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 2: Name one likely error with compose performance, correct it, and explain why the correction helps a reader or audience.\n\nParent: Marking notes: Require independently produced work with a specific supporting detail. / Require misconception + correction + purpose-linked reason..","pass":1,"pass_mark":0.9,"planner_fields":null,"planner_intro":null,"planner_title":null,"printable_resource":null,"quiz":[{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Strong answer: Ordered pieces, ''test speaker'', ''sing unaccompanied if app fails.'' This matches the lesson skill for compose performance.","options":["Copy the example artwork or script and call that independent work.","Strong answer: Ordered pieces, ''test speaker'', ''sing unaccompanied if app fails.''","First hearing the mix onstage with an audience waiting. Soundcheck earlier.","Say it looks nice with no element or technique named."],"question":"Write a two-item setlist with one tech-check item and one backup plan. Which response is most accurate?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"First hearing the mix onstage with an audience waiting. Soundcheck earlier. That misconception weakens accuracy; the other choices align with the lesson idea.","options":["Strong answer: Ordered pieces, ''test speaker'', ''sing unaccompanied if app fails.''","Careful use of setlist with clear evidence.","First hearing the mix onstage with an audience waiting. Soundcheck earlier.","Performing compositions needs a setlist order, instrument/tech check and a simple stage plot showing who stands where and which device is used. Do a…"],"question":"Which statement is a common mistake when practising compose performance?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Understanding is shown by new evidence and named setlist, not by copying the model.","options":["Invent a sacred First Nations design without permission or guidance.","Apply the idea with new evidence and name the setlist used.","Repeat the worked example wording with no new evidence.","Choose randomly because any option could be right."],"question":"A learner is practising compose performance. Which approach best shows understanding?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"Strong answer: Ordered pieces, ''test speaker'', ''sing unaccompanied if app fails.'' uses elements, techniques and audience effect appropriately for this lesson.","options":["First hearing the mix onstage with an audience waiting. Soundcheck earlier.","Say it looks nice with no element or technique named.","Copy the example artwork or script and call that independent work.","Strong answer: Ordered pieces, ''test speaker'', ''sing unaccompanied if app fails.''"],"question":"Which response best shows careful thinking about compose performance?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Strong answers name specific evidence and what it shows.","options":["Name a specific source, cue or example and say what it shows about compose performance.","Make a bigger claim without naming any source or cue.","Copy a classmate’s sentence with no local detail.","First hearing the mix onstage with an audience waiting. Soundcheck earlier."],"question":"Which habit strengthens evidence about setlist?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"The stronger choice matches the taught idea with concrete detail.","options":["Invent a sacred First Nations design without permission or guidance.","Say it looks nice with no element or technique named.","Example: Setlist 1) rhythm body piece 2) app loop song. Tech check: charge tablet, test cable, backup clap version ready.","First hearing the mix onstage with an audience waiting. Soundcheck earlier."],"question":"Using this lesson idea — Performing compositions needs a setlist order, instrument/tech check and a simple stage plot showing who… — which choice is best?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Respect and accuracy mean checking evidence and honouring limits/protocols.","options":["Check facts/cues, acknowledge limits, and avoid inventing details.","Invent missing details to make the answer sound complete.","Ignore safety or cultural protocols to finish faster.","Treat every online claim as equally reliable."],"question":"Which action shows respect and accuracy together?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Independence requires a new example that still uses the skill.","options":["Perform your composition with setlist and tech check complete. Note what the backup plan was even if unused.","Retype the worked example with no new example.","Copy the example artwork or script and call that independent work.","First hearing the mix onstage with an audience waiting. Soundcheck earlier."],"question":"Which task best shows independent use of compose performance?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"explanation":"Independent evidence on new material demonstrates the skill; copying the model does not.","marking_guide":"Require independently produced work with a specific supporting detail.","question":"Produce a fresh example demonstrating compose performance on new material (not the worked model). Explain the particular words, sources or choices that make it work.","sample_answer":"Original response on new material: Strong answer: Ordered pieces, ''test speaker'', ''sing unaccompanied if app fails.'' Reasoning: I used compose performance by attending to setlist rather than copying the worked model.","type":"short_answer"},{"explanation":"A useful correction changes the inaccurate idea or method and explains why.","marking_guide":"Require misconception + correction + purpose-linked reason.","question":"Name one likely error with compose performance, correct it, and explain why the correction helps a reader or audience.","sample_answer":"Common error: First hearing the mix onstage with an audience waiting. Soundcheck earlier. Correction: Strong answer: Ordered pieces, ''test speaker'', ''sing unaccompanied if app fails.'' Why: the correction restores accurate use of compose performance.","type":"short_answer"}],"resources":null,"response_prompt":"Include your independent artwork or performance notes and reflection, with reasons where requested.","review_status":"unreviewed","seed_key":"s2-arts-y4-w30-l1","sort_activity":null,"source_note":"Proposed Stage 2 NESA Creative Arts alignment using catalogue outcome codes (CA2-*); content-point mapping remains pending. First Nations arts content requires local Aboriginal educator or Custodian guidance before acceptance; do not invent sacred designs.","spelling":null,"spelling_focus":null,"stage":"S2","stage_hints":{"accept":["Today you will practise compose performance.","Read the mission before you start making or performing.","Keep the audience effect of your choice in view."],"guided":["Attempt the guided prompt without looking ahead.","Afterwards, compare your reasons with the feedback.","Adjust anything that does not name an effect clearly."],"learn":["Study how the first demonstration is built.","Point to the element or technique that carries the idea.","Then write the reason without copying every sentence."],"quiz":["Read every option before you choose.","Eliminate answers that ignore elements, safety or respectful practice.","Prefer a named artistic reason over a guess that merely looks colourful."],"submit":["Confirm that your choice and reason are both present.","Proofread element names and safety notes.","Make sure the final evidence matches the lesson purpose."],"teach0":["Read the stage title and find the worked example.","Name one exact element, technique or cue before you decide.","Think through the small prompt before opening the comparison."],"teach1":["Return to the example and list the key artistic choices.","Say what each choice does for the artwork or audience.","A final praise word alone is weaker than a named effect."],"teach2":["Compare a weak choice with a stronger one.","Change the element or technique, not only the decoration.","Name the mistake you are repairing."],"teach3":["Choose a fresh subject or piece that still uses the same skill.","Write one reason in your own words.","Do not retype the worked example as your answer."],"write":["Follow every part of the independent instructions.","Include original work notes and a short reflection.","Save work that shows the skill on new material."]},"subject":"Music","success_criteria":["I can use compose performance with a specific example from this lesson.","I can identify setlist and explain why it matters.","I can practise tech check independently on a new prompt.","I can notice stage plot needs and correct a likely mistake."],"suspense_builder":null,"teach_steps":[{"check":{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"Performing compositions needs a setlist order, instrument/tech check and a simple stage plot showing who stands where and which device is used. Do a soundcheck at performance volume. Have a backup unplugged version if tech fails. Supported responses name the element or…","options":["An answer copied without understanding.","A guess with no artistic reason.","Performing compositions needs a setlist order, instrument/tech check and a simple stage plot showing who stands where and which device is used. Do a soundcheck at performance volume. Have a backup unplugged version if tech fails.","A comment that only says it looks nice with no element named."],"question":"Which choice best shows accurate use of this idea about compose performance?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nExample: Setlist 1) rhythm body piece 2) app loop song. Tech check: charge tablet, test cable, backup clap version ready.\n\nTRY FIRST\nWrite a two-item setlist with one tech-check item and one backup plan.\n\nFEEDBACK\nStrong answer: Ordered pieces, ''test speaker'', ''sing unaccompanied if app fails.''","explain":"Performing compositions needs a setlist order, instrument/tech check and a simple stage plot showing who stands where and which device is used. Do a soundcheck at performance volume. Have a backup unplugged version if tech fails.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner make intentional visual, music, drama or dance choices and name their effect, rather than saying an artwork is simply “nice”. Keep every claim linked to an element or technique.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the worked example and name the elements, techniques or performance choices that carry the idea. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. For movement or instruments, use a clear space, ask an adult to be nearby and stop if anything feels unsafe. You may always describe a choice instead of performing it. One deliberate artistic choice with a named effect is more useful than a longer praise sentence.","icon":"📖","notice":"First hearing the mix onstage with an audience waiting. Soundcheck earlier. Name the element or technique and its effect, not just decoration.","title":"Understand and demonstrate","visual":[{"alt":"Performance prep.","caption":"Test early.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Setlist</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">order of pieces</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Soundcheck</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">before audience</text></g></svg>"}],"visual_before":[{"episode":{"scenes":[{"bg":"room","lines":[{"text":"I can see the example, but I am not sure which artistic choice matters most.","who":"pip"},{"text":"Name the element, technique or performance choice and the effect it creates before you decide.","who":"juno"},{"text":"I will try the prompt myself, then compare with the feedback.","who":"pip"},{"pause_after":true,"text":"Pause here. Use this example: Example: Setlist 1) rhythm body piece 2) app loop song. Tech check: charge tablet, test cable, backup clap version ready Then write your own artistic reason.","who":"juno"}]}],"title":"Talk through the first model","transcript":"Pip: I can see the example, but I am not sure which artistic choice matters most.\nJuno: Name the element, technique or performance choice and the effect it creates before you decide.\nPip: I will try the prompt myself, then compare with the feedback.\nJuno: Pause here. Use this example: Example: Setlist 1) rhythm body piece 2) app loop song. Tech check: charge tablet, test cable, backup clap version ready Then write your own artistic reason."}}]},{"check":{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Make the arts idea visible: name the elem