e artistic choice","visual":[{"alt":"Tech failsafes.","caption":"Always have a plan B.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Backup</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">unplugged plan</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Stage plot</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">who where</text></g></svg>"}]},{"check":{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"Use an intentionally weak or disrespectful arts choice as a comparison. Name the specific error, then show a clearer or more respectful choice. Supported responses name the element or technique and its effect.","options":["A comment that only says it looks nice with no element named.","An answer copied without understanding.","A guess with no artistic reason.","Use an intentionally weak or disrespectful arts choice as a comparison. Name the specific error, then show a clearer or more respectful choice."],"question":"Which choice best shows accurate use of this idea about compose performance?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nFirst hearing the mix onstage with an audience waiting. Soundcheck earlier. Here is a more helpful example: Example: Setlist 1) rhythm body piece 2) app loop song. Tech check: charge tablet, test cable, backup clap version ready.\n\nTRY FIRST\nDescribe why the warned-against choice weakens the work, then write a stronger choice with a reason.\n\nFEEDBACK\nStrong answer: Ordered pieces, ''test speaker'', ''sing unaccompanied if app fails.''","explain":"Use an intentionally weak or disrespectful arts choice as a comparison. Name the specific error, then show a clearer or more respectful choice.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner make intentional visual, music, drama or dance choices and name their effect, rather 